If a patient has a fibromyalgia then it is possible that a tricyclic-antidepressant improves a pain and improves a function and improves a quality-of-life.
If a patient has a fibromyalgia then it is possible that an SNRI-antidepressant improves a pain and improves a function and improves a quality-of-life.
If a patient has a fibromyalgia then it is possible that an NSAID improves a pain and improves a function and improves a quality-of-life.
If a patient has a fibromyalgia then it is possible that a pregabalin improves a pain and improves a function and improves a quality-of-life.
If a patient has a fibromyalgia then it is possible that a gabapentin improves a pain and improves a function and improves a quality-of-life.
A tricyclic-antidepressant-example is an amitriptyline-example.
An SNRI-antidepressant-example includes a duloxetine-example and includes a milnacipran-example.
An NSAID-example is a topical-diclofenac-example.
